    {
        "id": 2252233,
        "position": 4,
        "description": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_134300000000000001/attachments/27286931/dp_app.css\"><p><span data-teams=\"true\">This is an assignment to simply write your topic for the term paper (Assignment 5) and have it approved by the TA.<br>Since this is a Text Submission, the TA will reply to your submission here with an \"approved\" or with a recommendation to adjust the topic.<br>Feel free to add pointers or notes to convey the scope of the topic as needed.<br><br><strong>How to Choose a Topic for Your Term Essay</strong><br><strong>1) Consider the Scope of Your Paper</strong><br>The assignment requires <strong>4 to 5 pages</strong> of content. This means:<br>The topic should be complex enough to discuss in depth but not so broad that it becomes unmanageable.<br>It should allow you to cover aspects like history, impact (both positive and negative), and future implications.<br>For example:<br><strong>Too broad</strong>: \u201cCybersecurity Threats\u201d (Too many threats to cover in 4-5 pages)<br><strong>Too narrow</strong>: \u201cSecurity Flaws in a Specific Android App\u201d (May not provide enough material)<br><strong>Balanced</strong>: \u201cThe Ethical and Security Challenges of AI-Powered Deepfake Technology\u201d<br><br><strong>2) Align With Your Major</strong><br>Your topic must relate to contemporary issues within <strong>computer science, software engineering, or computer engineering</strong>. Think about areas of interest within your major.<br><br><strong>3) Identify a Type of Essay</strong><br>Your essay should fit one of the three categories:<br><strong>Explanatory</strong>: Describes a contemporary issue without taking sides.<br>Example: \u201cThe Evolution of Cryptography in Data Security\u201d<br><strong>Analytical</strong>: Weighs pros and cons.<br>Example: \u201cCloud Computing: Balancing Efficiency and Security Risks\u201d<br><strong>Argumentative</strong>: Takes a stance and argues for it.<br>Example: \u201cWhy All Consumer IoT Devices Should Have Mandatory Security Regulations<br><br><strong>4) Submit The Topic Here and Get Approved</strong><br>Start working as soon as you get your topic approved.</span></p><script src=\"https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_134300000000000001/attachments/27286930/dp_app.js\"></script>",
